WEBVTT

00:00:02.319 --> 00:00:27.320
I just intercepted the file.

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:30.320
Yeah, of course I deleted any trace of it.

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:32.320
This isn't the first time I've done something like this.

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:35.780
I'll see in a few.

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:45.390
Get after me.

00:00:45.390 --> 00:01:08.739
And is this when you're supposed to swoop in and save me?

00:01:08.739 --> 00:01:17.269
No pepper spray?

00:01:17.269 --> 00:01:22.920
The city's a dangerous place.

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:28.340
You should be prepared.

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:29.340
You can have my wallet.

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:31.340
You know that's not what I'm after.

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:38.420
Next time, maybe you'll think twice before you steal what doesn't belong to you.

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:39.420
Finders keepers.

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:41.420
I like the look.

00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:43.420
Italian.

00:01:43.420 --> 00:01:46.420
Why? You thinking of trading in your tights?

00:01:46.420 --> 00:03:58.539
Good morning.

00:03:58.539 --> 00:04:00.539
Hi.

00:04:00.539 --> 00:05:05.310
Dina Lance, the word of justice, the right-wing hawk of the airways.

00:05:05.310 --> 00:05:08.310
You're all dressed up, heading to an execution.

00:05:08.310 --> 00:05:11.310
If you ever did any fact-checking Lois,

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:14.310
you'd know that the state outlawed those years ago.

00:05:14.310 --> 00:05:16.310
I'm sure you'll get over it someday.

00:05:16.310 --> 00:05:17.310
Well, if you're so in the know,

00:05:17.310 --> 00:05:23.310
If you're so in the know, then I suppose you know that your limousine Liberal Casanova has resurfaced,

00:05:23.310 --> 00:05:49.029
minus a certain shrill arm trophy.

00:05:49.029 --> 00:05:51.029
Looking for a new hairdo?

00:05:51.029 --> 00:05:53.029
Let me guess, Hamm and Swiss?

00:05:53.029 --> 00:05:54.029
Your favorite?

00:05:54.029 --> 00:05:56.029
No, actually. Not at all.

00:05:56.029 --> 00:05:59.029
Which I think I've mentioned three times this week, but thanks anyway.

00:05:59.029 --> 00:06:01.029
I just can't hang around that house anymore, Chloe.

00:06:01.029 --> 00:06:04.029
Knowing that Phantom was living my life with Lana for over a month,

00:06:04.029 --> 00:06:07.029
while I was trapped in the fortress, I know we looked alike,

00:06:07.029 --> 00:06:09.029
but she really couldn't tell the difference.

00:06:09.029 --> 00:06:10.029
And then she tells him,

00:06:10.029 --> 00:06:13.029
they belong together. Does that mean she doesn't feel that way about me?

00:06:13.029 --> 00:06:19.660
Well, she isn't exactly the same girl you used to trip all over in high school either.

00:06:19.660 --> 00:06:23.839
I don't want to talk about this anymore.

00:06:23.839 --> 00:06:26.839
Right. I'm sorry, I brought it up.

00:06:26.839 --> 00:06:32.120
Any luck locating the brain-interactive construct?

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:34.120
Not since you asked me yesterday.

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:37.399
What happened to your face?

00:06:37.399 --> 00:06:40.399
First of all, did you seriously not notice this until just now?

00:06:40.399 --> 00:06:44.899
Don't worry, Clark. I'm fine.

00:06:44.899 --> 00:06:46.899
Chloe.

00:06:46.899 --> 00:06:53.399
All right. I've sort of been doing this side.

00:06:53.399 --> 00:06:56.399
have been doing this sidekick side job for Oliver.

00:06:56.399 --> 00:06:57.399
What?

00:06:57.399 --> 00:07:00.399
Look, Clark, a girl has got to pay her bills.

00:07:00.399 --> 00:07:02.399
And, I mean, let's face it.

00:07:02.399 --> 00:07:04.399
You kind of fill my pro bono quota.

00:07:04.399 --> 00:07:06.399
His missions are dangerous.

00:07:06.399 --> 00:07:07.399
And the fact he's taking you with him...

00:07:07.399 --> 00:07:11.649
No, no, no, it was just internet interception

00:07:11.649 --> 00:07:15.649
that ended up having a vicious ninja lady attached to it

00:07:15.649 --> 00:07:18.649
who chased me onto the roof and then almost beheaded me

00:07:18.649 --> 00:07:21.649
and went repelling over the side of the building,

00:07:21.649 --> 00:07:23.649
which I've got to admit was really smoking cool.

00:07:23.649 --> 00:07:24.649
Cool.

00:07:24.649 --> 00:07:27.310
Who was she?

00:07:27.310 --> 00:07:40.379
You put Chloe in danger.

00:07:40.379 --> 00:07:44.339
So, I take it, we're skipping over the whole...

00:07:44.339 --> 00:07:46.339
Hello. Good to see again, part of the conversation.

00:07:46.339 --> 00:07:50.339
If you and your crew want to go out there and put your own lives on the line, that's fine.

00:07:50.339 --> 00:07:52.339
Go ahead. But not Chloe.

00:07:52.339 --> 00:07:55.339
Smart doesn't help when someone's trying to attack you on a rooftop.

00:07:55.339 --> 00:07:59.339
First of all, I don't think our leather fetish mystery woman was trying to kill Chloe.

00:07:59.339 --> 00:08:01.339
She shouldn't have been in danger at all.

00:08:01.339 --> 00:08:04.339
Secondly, Chloe's in danger like every other week with you by her side, Clark.

00:08:04.339 --> 00:08:07.339
You're the one who goes into things without giving in a second thought.

00:08:07.339 --> 00:08:11.339
Why don't you try to think about someone other than yourself for once?

00:08:11.339 --> 00:08:12.339
I'm selfish?

00:08:12.339 --> 00:08:16.579
You know, some of us sacrifice being with the people that we really care about

00:08:16.579 --> 00:08:18.579
so that we can go make a difference.

00:08:18.579 --> 00:08:19.579
What do you do?

00:08:19.579 --> 00:08:22.579
You sit around in domestic bliss curled up on a couch

00:08:22.579 --> 00:08:25.579
while the world of trouble spins outside your door.

00:08:25.579 --> 00:08:41.970
This blonde woman, Chloe said she shattered your arrows.

00:08:41.970 --> 00:08:46.970
Not my proudest moment, but yeah,

00:08:46.970 --> 00:08:49.970
she must have some kind of sound frequency control.

00:08:49.970 --> 00:08:52.970
all the noise went muffled right before it happened.

00:08:52.970 --> 00:08:58.110
The files she stole, Chloe said she didn't know what it was.

00:08:58.110 --> 00:09:00.110
I didn't tell her what it was.

00:09:00.110 --> 00:09:04.110
We've intercepted Lex's latest project.

00:09:04.110 --> 00:09:06.110
It's a photo file.

00:09:06.110 --> 00:09:09.110
And this masked woman just happened to show up.

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:22.669
Maybe Lex has a blonde sidekick of his own.

00:09:22.669 --> 00:09:25.669
I usually mind when someone sits in the chair, but

00:09:25.669 --> 00:09:28.669
I'm a little distracted to care at the moment.

00:09:28.669 --> 00:09:31.669
I don't take to the morally murky.

00:09:31.669 --> 00:09:32.669
I'm not taking to the morally murky.

00:09:32.669 --> 00:09:33.669
they pay you.

00:09:33.669 --> 00:09:38.330
You know my standards.

00:09:38.330 --> 00:09:41.330
No matter how rich you are, you don't deserve to be robbed.

00:09:41.330 --> 00:09:46.409
And you, Richie, are a lucky man.

00:09:46.409 --> 00:09:49.409
If you stopped whoever's been hacking into my trade secrets,

00:09:49.409 --> 00:09:52.409
I consider myself very lucky.

00:09:52.409 --> 00:09:54.409
Your file almost fell into the wrong hands.

00:09:54.409 --> 00:09:57.409
I had a little run-in with an emerald archer.

00:09:57.409 --> 00:10:00.409
Green Arrow?

00:10:00.409 --> 00:10:02.409
I wasn't expecting company.

00:10:02.409 --> 00:10:06.409
You think you can find them again?

00:10:06.409 --> 00:10:07.409
If I had a good room.

00:10:07.409 --> 00:10:08.409
reason?

00:10:08.409 --> 00:10:12.409
They've been breaking in and setting off bombs at my work sites.

00:10:12.409 --> 00:10:14.409
They belong in prison.

00:10:14.409 --> 00:10:30.220
You bring me Green Arrow, and I will make it worth your while.

00:10:30.220 --> 00:10:32.220
Like this back as soon as possible.

00:10:32.220 --> 00:10:35.139
Thanks.

00:10:35.139 --> 00:10:39.139
I, uh, I've been calling the farm, but no announcers.

00:10:39.139 --> 00:10:42.139
It's as if the place has been abandoned.

00:10:42.139 --> 00:10:47.500
Are we of caller ID?

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:53.500
The, um, editor of the Daily Planet, Grant Gabriel.

00:10:54.500 --> 00:10:56.500
He's been shot and killed.

00:10:56.500 --> 00:10:58.500
I'm a guess.

00:10:58.500 --> 00:11:01.500
You think Lex is behind it?

00:11:01.500 --> 00:11:04.500
I do, yes. I think it's why he bought the paper.

00:11:04.500 --> 00:11:11.580
It's the beauty of a divorce, Lionel.

00:11:11.580 --> 00:11:14.580
Covering up Lex's baggage is no longer my problem.

00:11:14.580 --> 00:11:16.580
I don't want to cover it up, Lana.

00:11:16.580 --> 00:11:18.580
I want proof.

00:11:18.580 --> 00:11:20.580
I know you can get it for me.

00:11:20.580 --> 00:11:24.580
Lex and I have kind of suspended tea time together.

00:11:24.580 --> 00:11:28.580
I know you have hours of footage, spy footage on him.

00:11:28.580 --> 00:11:29.580
on him.

00:11:29.580 --> 00:11:33.580
I'm sure I can find something that will incriminate him.

00:11:33.580 --> 00:11:36.580
What leads you to believe that I would help you?

00:11:36.580 --> 00:11:41.580
Several weeks ago, you held a very sick woman hostage.

00:11:41.580 --> 00:11:43.580
I was trying to help her.

00:11:43.580 --> 00:11:46.580
And how did that work out for you, bypassing the hospital?

00:11:46.580 --> 00:11:48.580
Oh, oh, yes, that's right.

00:11:48.580 --> 00:11:51.580
She died in your care.

00:11:51.580 --> 00:11:56.580
You were very quick to share all this with Clark's doppelganger, but...

00:11:56.580 --> 00:12:06.230
Why didn't you tell Clark?

00:12:06.230 --> 00:12:08.230
Call me when you're ready for movie night.

00:12:08.230 --> 00:13:25.879
This vigilante woman attacked Chloe.

00:13:25.879 --> 00:13:32.139
I thought maybe you'd know if she was connected to Lex.

00:13:32.139 --> 00:13:40.450
It's kind of interesting that everyone was so quick to turn me into Lady Macbeth when they found out I was watching Lex.

00:13:40.450 --> 00:13:43.450
And yet, you're the second person to ask for my help today.

00:13:43.450 --> 00:13:50.919
The second person?

00:13:50.919 --> 00:13:53.919
She's not in any of the old footage I would have remembered the mask.

00:13:53.919 --> 00:14:01.639
I appreciate it.

00:14:01.639 --> 00:14:12.440
Clark, when you were gone, I was treating this woman.

00:14:12.440 --> 00:14:13.440
She was catatonic.

00:14:13.440 --> 00:14:17.440
She was catatonic after Brainiac infected her.

00:14:17.440 --> 00:14:19.440
What do you mean treating?

00:14:19.440 --> 00:14:20.440
Monitoring her.

00:14:20.440 --> 00:14:24.419
Until she passed away.

00:14:24.419 --> 00:14:27.220
She passed away?

00:14:27.220 --> 00:14:29.220
There wasn't anything else we could do.

00:14:29.220 --> 00:14:31.220
Her mind was already gone.

00:14:31.220 --> 00:14:33.220
We were just looking for clues.

00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:35.220
Who's we?

00:14:35.220 --> 00:14:44.220
You told the Phantom this?

00:14:44.220 --> 00:14:46.220
Lana, why do you bother telling me now?

00:14:46.220 --> 00:14:51.870
Lionel's holding it over my head.

00:14:51.870 --> 00:14:56.340
I can't do this, Lana.

00:14:56.340 --> 00:14:58.340
You're only honest with me when you're threatened.

00:14:58.340 --> 00:15:00.340
In a few weeks with him...

00:15:00.340 --> 00:15:02.340
I don't know what else to say to you.

00:15:02.340 --> 00:15:04.340
I thought that he was you.

00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:07.340
You're supposed to know me better than anyone.

00:15:07.340 --> 00:15:09.340
And that's why you're here with me right now.

00:15:09.340 --> 00:15:11.340
But it was easier with him, wasn't it?

00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:14.139
Yes.

00:15:14.139 --> 00:15:16.139
It was easier, Clark.

00:15:16.139 --> 00:15:18.139
He was more affectionate.

00:15:18.139 --> 00:15:20.139
He was more understanding.

00:15:20.139 --> 00:15:23.139
Is that really what you want to hear?

00:15:23.139 --> 00:15:30.179
I can't even look at you without you taking it the wrong way.

00:15:30.179 --> 00:15:32.179
Because you're looking at me like you wished I was someone else.

00:15:32.179 --> 00:15:33.179
someone else.

00:15:33.179 --> 00:15:40.210
Every transgression that I have made,

00:15:40.210 --> 00:15:44.210
you have answered with a hypocritical judgment.

00:15:44.210 --> 00:15:47.210
No one can live up to your self-righteous standards.

00:15:47.210 --> 00:15:54.440
Have any idea how it feels to wake up every morning,

00:15:54.440 --> 00:15:59.440
knowing that you're going to fail in the eyes of the only person you've ever really loved.

00:15:59.440 --> 00:16:04.139
And you're the one who fell in love with Lex.

00:16:04.139 --> 00:16:06.139
And then fell for that killer.

00:16:06.139 --> 00:16:18.120
I don't think it's me you can't face.

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:56.059
Give me a call.

00:16:56.059 --> 00:17:00.539
Lois?

00:17:00.539 --> 00:17:09.390
is going to be harder than I thought.

00:17:09.390 --> 00:17:10.390
That's for breaking my heart.

00:17:10.390 --> 00:17:11.390
Really?

00:17:11.390 --> 00:17:14.390
Because it felt like it was for not calling when I got back into town.

00:17:14.390 --> 00:17:17.390
That one will come when you least expected.

00:17:17.390 --> 00:17:19.390
Would you put a shirt on or something?

00:17:19.390 --> 00:17:32.700
Well, at least I know why I got canned from your speed dial.

00:17:32.700 --> 00:17:36.700
The whole, uh, jumping to conclusions thing before getting the full story,

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:37.700
how's I working out for you?

00:17:37.700 --> 00:17:39.700
Huge time saver.

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:40.700
The dinner's for you.

00:17:40.700 --> 00:17:49.259
I knew you'd be on my doorstep.

00:17:49.259 --> 00:17:53.640
And if you weren't, I'd have been on yours.

00:17:53.640 --> 00:17:54.640
I've been on yours.

00:17:54.640 --> 00:17:58.549
I missed you.

00:17:58.549 --> 00:18:04.670
You could possibly know.

00:18:04.670 --> 00:18:12.220
If you think the glistening muscle answering the door

00:18:12.220 --> 00:18:15.220
in your bare chest routine was gonna work,

00:18:15.220 --> 00:18:27.549
you were dead on.

00:18:27.549 --> 00:18:45.900
You're all I could think about.

00:18:45.900 --> 00:18:46.900
Nice try.

00:18:46.900 --> 00:18:50.900
Does that work on all the fish net, leather-clad blondes you have stashed on the balcony?

00:18:50.900 --> 00:19:13.509
Get out!

00:19:13.509 --> 00:19:23.730
Ollie!

00:19:23.730 --> 00:19:24.730
Oh my god.

00:19:24.730 --> 00:19:54.210
Lois?

00:19:54.210 --> 00:19:59.640
Oh, don't even think of looking at me right now.

00:19:59.640 --> 00:20:02.640
So, in all those nights together, somewhere between

00:20:02.640 --> 00:20:05.140
Somewhere between brushing teeth and spooning in the sheets,

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:07.140
you didn't think that it might be a good time to mention

00:20:07.140 --> 00:20:09.140
that you prowled the streets with green leather

00:20:09.140 --> 00:20:11.140
and a compound bow?

00:20:11.140 --> 00:20:14.140
I don't usually bring the compound bow.

00:20:14.140 --> 00:20:16.140
Oh, so now he's a funny hero.

00:20:16.140 --> 00:20:19.140
I can't believe you didn't tell me you were Green Arrow.

00:20:19.140 --> 00:20:23.140
Hard to imagine why when you're taking it so well.

00:20:23.140 --> 00:20:25.640
You'd think the lacerating ropes and Platinum Fembot

00:20:25.640 --> 00:20:29.140
might have something to do with my lack of empathy?

00:20:29.140 --> 00:20:30.140
So what?

00:20:30.140 --> 00:20:32.140
Little Lolly got bored with Dodgeball and P.E.

00:20:32.140 --> 00:20:35.519
decided to play William Tell?

00:20:35.519 --> 00:20:36.519
Whoa.

00:20:36.519 --> 00:20:37.519
Wait a second.

00:20:37.519 --> 00:20:41.019
I kissed Green Arrow last year when you were standing there with me

00:20:41.019 --> 00:20:42.019
in the alley.

00:20:42.019 --> 00:20:43.019
Yeah.

00:20:43.019 --> 00:20:45.019
I remember that with precise detail.

00:20:45.019 --> 00:20:46.519
I can't believe you.

00:20:46.519 --> 00:20:49.019
You who are supposedly my boyfriend arranged for me

00:20:49.019 --> 00:20:51.019
to be lip-locked with some wannabe hero.

00:20:51.019 --> 00:20:53.019
Lois!

00:20:53.019 --> 00:20:55.019
Oh, how do you put up with that?

00:20:55.019 --> 00:20:58.019
I don't know what it is you want for me,

00:20:58.019 --> 00:21:01.019
but I'm hoping we just got off on the wrong foot.

00:21:01.019 --> 00:21:03.500
You can save your charm for your squawking

00:21:03.519 --> 00:21:04.519
Parrot over there.

00:21:04.519 --> 00:21:06.519
Whatever someone's paying you, I can beat it.

00:21:06.519 --> 00:21:08.519
You know, this is more than just about money, pretty boy.

00:21:08.519 --> 00:21:12.519
This is about something that you and your merry band of thieves might not understand.

00:21:12.519 --> 00:21:14.519
Justice.

00:21:14.519 --> 00:21:18.519
Lady Justice must be blinder than I thought she was if she's got you on her side.

00:21:18.519 --> 00:21:20.799
Just tell me this.

00:21:20.799 --> 00:21:24.799
What goes through the mind of a terrorist when he's about to set off a bomb in a factory?

00:21:24.799 --> 00:21:26.799
A terrorist?

00:21:26.799 --> 00:21:28.799
You really have it backwards.

00:21:28.799 --> 00:21:30.799
No one's ever been hurt.

00:21:30.799 --> 00:21:34.779
And Lexus factories aren't exactly producing Christmas toys for little girls and girls

00:21:34.799 --> 00:21:36.799
boys. I'm the good guy.

00:21:36.799 --> 00:21:48.109
Isn't everybody?

00:21:48.109 --> 00:21:50.109
When I say I'm gonna do something, I always deliver.

00:21:50.109 --> 00:21:52.109
Now it's your turn.

00:21:52.109 --> 00:21:54.109
You want your boy over here?

00:21:54.109 --> 00:21:56.109
Start the wire transfer.

00:21:56.109 --> 00:22:17.519
In case you can't see it, the white flag is flying, so don't even

00:22:17.519 --> 00:22:19.519
think about going off on me again.

00:22:19.519 --> 00:22:21.519
I'm sorry for being so hard on you.

00:22:21.519 --> 00:22:24.519
What about the Oliver thing? I just don't want to see you getting hurt?

00:22:24.519 --> 00:22:27.519
Well, we could all breathe easier if we could find a lead on blonde ambition,

00:22:27.519 --> 00:22:29.519
but right now I got zero.

00:22:29.519 --> 00:22:32.829
A lot of Mike.

00:22:32.829 --> 00:22:34.829
Twist? Okay.

00:22:34.829 --> 00:22:37.829
She doesn't have any footage linking Lexi the attacker,

00:22:37.829 --> 00:22:39.829
but she was able to keep track of his projects,

00:22:39.829 --> 00:22:42.829
but piggybacking on the server from Luther Mansion.

00:22:42.829 --> 00:22:48.069
Of course. Right in front of my face.

00:22:48.069 --> 00:22:50.069
Our silent Cybrin knew I was making the interception

00:22:50.069 --> 00:22:53.069
because she was on the Daily Planet server.

00:22:53.069 --> 00:22:56.069
Can you access who logged on last night?

00:22:56.069 --> 00:22:58.069
Yeah, I can't believe I didn't see that.

00:22:58.069 --> 00:23:00.069
The negligent go-to girl strikes again.

00:23:00.069 --> 00:23:03.049
Chalk another one up for the new and improved

00:23:03.069 --> 00:23:04.069
model.

00:23:04.069 --> 00:23:09.069
Lana did come through, but I'm not about to let Oliver poach the best sidekick in town.

00:23:09.069 --> 00:23:16.349
Dina Lance was the only woman logged on last night.

00:23:16.349 --> 00:23:18.349
That doesn't help us much.

00:23:18.349 --> 00:23:19.349
Why?

00:23:19.349 --> 00:23:20.349
Because she's not blonde?

00:23:20.349 --> 00:23:22.349
Please, Clark.

00:23:22.349 --> 00:23:26.819
The new bad girl could be as blonde as I really am.

00:23:26.819 --> 00:23:28.819
There we go. Raven black.

00:23:28.819 --> 00:23:32.509
Canary yellow.

00:23:32.509 --> 00:23:34.509
Maybe we should call her the yellow raven.

00:23:34.509 --> 00:23:37.509
A canary has a better ring to it.

00:23:37.509 --> 00:23:41.509
This makes so much sense.

00:23:41.509 --> 00:23:42.509
I mean.

00:23:42.509 --> 00:23:44.509
Dina's slogan is the word of justice.

00:23:44.509 --> 00:23:48.509
Family of cops, hardline view of crime and corruption.

00:23:48.509 --> 00:23:50.509
What are you doing?

00:23:50.509 --> 00:23:52.509
Earning back my stripes.

00:23:52.509 --> 00:23:54.509
I just hacked into Dina's computer,

00:23:54.509 --> 00:23:57.509
and it looks like there is a transfer in occurrence

00:23:57.509 --> 00:24:05.049
to her bank account right now.

00:24:05.049 --> 00:24:07.049
I always said the file you intercepted the other night

00:24:07.049 --> 00:24:09.049
was from Lex. Can you block this transfer?

00:24:09.049 --> 00:24:10.049
Hmm.

00:24:10.049 --> 00:24:17.349
Cut off the air supply, so she'll have to surface.

00:24:17.349 --> 00:24:18.349
Got it.

00:24:18.349 --> 00:24:35.730
Missing your payoff?

00:24:35.730 --> 00:24:38.730
I guess there's no honor among thieves.

00:24:38.730 --> 00:24:39.730
Let me guess.

00:24:39.730 --> 00:24:41.730
You're one of the green beans, little accomplices.

00:24:41.730 --> 00:24:44.730
And now that your boss is all tied up, you're out of work.

00:24:44.730 --> 00:24:46.730
What'd you do, then?

00:24:46.730 --> 00:24:50.359
Green Arrow isn't the villain here. Lex is.

00:24:50.359 --> 00:24:53.359
Even tycoons who buy out the press deserve justice.

00:24:53.359 --> 00:24:56.359
Is that the line you use to convince yourself you're on the right side?

00:24:56.359 --> 00:24:59.359
You know, you may not have experience this, that boy.

00:24:59.359 --> 00:25:01.359
But when you're on the right side, you don't have to do any convincing.

00:25:01.359 --> 00:25:02.359
Did it ever occur to you?

00:25:02.359 --> 00:25:05.359
There might be a reason why the Green Arrow was stealing from Lex?

00:25:05.359 --> 00:25:07.359
Actually, it didn't occur to me that anything about

00:25:07.359 --> 00:25:09.359
about Queen was reasonable.

00:25:09.359 --> 00:25:11.359
Sorry, Green Arrow.

00:25:11.359 --> 00:25:14.359
Next time you're a gun for hire, do your research.

00:25:14.359 --> 00:25:22.339
Why would a rich guy like Oliver waste his time intercepting files for the fun of it?

00:25:22.339 --> 00:25:26.640
What line did Lex feed you?

00:25:26.640 --> 00:25:30.640
The you and your little gang were breaking into his plants all over the world, stealing trade secrets.

00:25:30.640 --> 00:25:32.640
I'm guessing he didn't tell you what those secrets were.

00:25:32.640 --> 00:25:36.529
Where's Oliver?

00:25:36.529 --> 00:26:38.160
Oh, aren't you clever? You managed to sneak in.

00:26:38.160 --> 00:26:40.160
Did you, uh, find anything?

00:26:40.160 --> 00:26:43.160
Didn't find anything linking Grant Gabriel's murder.

00:26:43.160 --> 00:26:50.700
to Lex, because I'm not looking.

00:26:50.700 --> 00:26:52.700
I think, Lana.

00:26:52.700 --> 00:26:56.700
You know what you've done, lying to Clark, deceiving him.

00:26:56.700 --> 00:26:59.700
Clark knows everything.

00:26:59.700 --> 00:27:02.700
And he will know everything from now.

00:27:02.700 --> 00:27:07.240
So I guess your cards are off the table.

00:27:07.240 --> 00:27:09.240
Well, it's obvious that you, uh,

00:27:09.240 --> 00:27:12.240
adopt it more than just the Luther name.

00:27:12.240 --> 00:27:17.240
What about the part of you that, uh,

00:27:17.240 --> 00:27:18.240
wanted to, uh,

00:27:18.240 --> 00:27:21.240
bring Lex to justice for all the evil that he's done?

00:27:21.240 --> 00:27:24.319
that he's done? Is that also off the table?

00:27:24.319 --> 00:27:27.119
Sometimes justice comes at too high a price.

00:27:28.240 --> 00:27:30.240
Like sacrificing my relationship with Clark

00:27:30.240 --> 00:27:33.240
because I wanted to see Lex pay for his sins.

00:27:33.240 --> 00:27:35.240
Why did you come here?

00:27:35.240 --> 00:27:38.240
I went to the edge, and Clark pulled me back.

00:27:38.240 --> 00:27:41.240
Trying to do the same thing for you.

00:27:41.240 --> 00:27:49.059
So this is because you have my best interests at heart.

00:27:49.059 --> 00:27:51.059
It's not about you.

00:27:51.059 --> 00:27:53.059
I'm trying to change.

00:27:53.059 --> 00:27:57.059
To be honest, to be the kind of person that Clark could love again.

00:27:57.059 --> 00:28:00.849
What game are you playing?

00:28:00.849 --> 00:28:03.849
Lex is living proof of what obsession can do.

00:28:03.849 --> 00:28:05.849
I know my son better than you.

00:28:05.849 --> 00:28:12.119
No, you don't. Be careful.

00:28:12.119 --> 00:28:40.289
Lois, what happened?

00:28:40.289 --> 00:28:42.289
This crazy woman attacked us.

00:28:42.289 --> 00:28:47.309
Why did some woman attack you and Oliver?

00:28:47.309 --> 00:28:48.309
Hey!

00:28:48.309 --> 00:28:51.309
Isn't the view spectacular? I never really noticed it before

00:28:51.309 --> 00:28:54.309
without the... all the blasts in the way.

00:28:54.309 --> 00:28:55.309
The view?

00:28:55.309 --> 00:28:58.039
You?

00:28:58.039 --> 00:28:59.039
I know.

00:28:59.039 --> 00:29:00.039
Can you believe this guy?

00:29:00.039 --> 00:29:01.039
A hydraulic walking closet?

00:29:01.039 --> 00:29:04.039
You're not going to find that in a sharper image catalog.

00:29:04.039 --> 00:29:06.039
Must be laundry day.

00:29:06.039 --> 00:29:09.039
I mean, who picks archery as a hobby?

00:29:09.039 --> 00:29:10.039
That's embarrassing.

00:29:10.039 --> 00:29:12.039
I'd keep my quiver in the closet, too.

00:29:12.039 --> 00:29:14.039
Lois, where is Oliver?

00:29:14.039 --> 00:29:16.039
I don't know.

00:29:16.039 --> 00:29:17.039
She knocked me out.

00:29:17.039 --> 00:29:28.000
When I came to you, they were both gone.

00:29:28.000 --> 00:29:34.230
I think you forgot a little green something at home?

00:29:34.230 --> 00:29:38.230
I'm not handing Green Arrow over to you until you can prove how bad he is.

00:29:38.230 --> 00:29:40.759
The fact that he's been.

00:29:40.759 --> 00:29:42.759
breaking into my plant seems sufficient.

00:29:42.759 --> 00:29:45.759
About those plants, I've been doing a little digging.

00:29:45.759 --> 00:29:48.759
It seems your auto parts factory doesn't sell any auto parts.

00:29:48.759 --> 00:29:51.759
And your tech warehouse doesn't distribute computers.

00:29:51.759 --> 00:29:54.759
Looks like you've been buying into his propaganda.

00:29:54.759 --> 00:29:58.759
I don't like being caught on the wrong side, which is what I'm on.

00:29:58.759 --> 00:29:59.759
Isn't it?

00:29:59.759 --> 00:30:02.759
You were never going to hand green arrow over to the police, were you?

00:30:02.759 --> 00:30:06.759
I'm not much for philosophical debates.

00:30:06.759 --> 00:30:08.759
I just want what I paid for.

00:30:08.759 --> 00:30:09.759
Well, then I guess it answers my question.

00:30:09.759 --> 00:30:12.759
was my question. I'm not handing him over.

00:30:12.759 --> 00:30:17.970
Where is he? Try looking over your shoulder.

00:30:17.970 --> 00:32:01.240
Slash green arrow. Any other hyphenates I need to know about?

00:32:01.240 --> 00:32:03.240
No, that's pretty much the bigie.

00:32:03.240 --> 00:32:16.779
Sorry. I never meant to hide who I was from you. I just...

00:32:16.779 --> 00:32:20.779
No, it's okay. I get it. You were just trying to protect me.

00:32:20.779 --> 00:32:27.420
And I gotta say, it clears up a lot.

00:32:27.420 --> 00:32:31.420
I never did make sense how you could blow off a haughty like me.

00:32:31.420 --> 00:32:43.670
Well, now that you know, really, really,

00:32:43.670 --> 00:32:54.589
hoping that I know my job takes me out of town a lot.

00:32:54.589 --> 00:32:56.589
On the weekends, there's a...

00:32:56.589 --> 00:33:04.029
Please give us another chance.

00:33:04.029 --> 00:33:13.200
I can make this work.

00:33:13.200 --> 00:33:14.200
I can't.

00:33:14.200 --> 00:33:17.200
You know, me and my big mouth, I can never keep a secret.

00:33:17.200 --> 00:33:19.200
I don't believe that.

00:33:19.200 --> 00:33:24.279
I've never been good at long-distance relationships.

00:33:24.279 --> 00:33:26.279
Come on, Lois.

00:33:26.279 --> 00:33:27.279
Okay.

00:33:27.279 --> 00:33:35.740
I share.

00:33:35.740 --> 00:33:37.740
But I don't want to wonder where you are every night.

00:33:37.740 --> 00:33:46.039
But good at the whole dual identity thing.

00:33:46.039 --> 00:33:58.630
Can't you?

00:33:58.630 --> 00:34:44.329
share you with the rest.

00:34:44.329 --> 00:34:46.329
Enter at your own caloric risk.

00:34:46.329 --> 00:34:50.219
How you doing?

00:34:50.219 --> 00:34:54.219
Aside from the metaphor, I was hoping Rocky Road would help, but nothing.

00:34:54.219 --> 00:35:00.900
Not a, not even a dent.

00:35:00.900 --> 00:35:06.530
You know, I thought Grant would help me get over Olly.

00:35:06.530 --> 00:35:10.530
And if that didn't end badly enough,

00:35:10.530 --> 00:35:15.530
the moment I saw Olly again, all those feelings just came rushing right back up.

00:35:15.530 --> 00:35:19.099
Maybe you can still work between you two.

00:35:19.099 --> 00:35:22.829
You don't know Olly like I do.

00:35:22.829 --> 00:35:24.829
There are parts of him you've never seen.

00:35:24.829 --> 00:35:28.170
That's a given.

00:35:28.170 --> 00:35:30.170
I mean sides of him.

00:35:30.170 --> 00:35:36.059
He's got this one side that I'm not sure I can live with.

00:35:36.059 --> 00:35:38.059
How would you know if you don't give a chance?

00:35:38.059 --> 00:35:41.059
We're not you and Lana. We're not the perfect couple.

00:35:41.059 --> 00:35:43.059
We are not destined for each other.

00:35:43.059 --> 00:35:45.059
Lois, this isn't like you.

00:35:45.059 --> 00:35:48.059
Normally when things get challenging, that's when you get interested.

00:35:48.059 --> 00:35:50.059
This is different.

00:35:50.059 --> 00:35:53.059
My dad was a general.

00:35:53.059 --> 00:35:55.059
He cared about me.

00:35:55.059 --> 00:35:56.059
He cared about me.

00:35:56.059 --> 00:35:58.059
But I learned really early that his role in the world

00:35:58.059 --> 00:36:01.059
was a lot more important than being a father.

00:36:01.059 --> 00:36:04.059
And you know what, for good reasons.

00:36:04.059 --> 00:36:07.059
And Ollie's life is demanding, too.

00:36:07.059 --> 00:36:11.880
Lois, just because someone's life is great responsibility

00:36:11.880 --> 00:36:14.880
doesn't mean your life has to take second place.

00:36:14.880 --> 00:36:19.920
Of course it does, Clark.

00:36:19.920 --> 00:36:22.920
Can you imagine what it would be like

00:36:22.920 --> 00:36:26.920
to look into somebody's eyes and know that their destiny is so much greater than yours

00:36:26.920 --> 00:36:29.920
that you will never compete.

00:36:29.920 --> 00:36:30.920
You will always.

00:36:30.920 --> 00:36:34.460
be left behind.

00:36:34.460 --> 00:36:36.460
That would be hard for anyone.

00:36:36.460 --> 00:36:37.460
But...

00:36:37.460 --> 00:36:40.460
No, I can't be left behind one more time.

00:36:40.460 --> 00:36:48.320
You know, where all these life is going,

00:36:48.320 --> 00:36:51.320
there's not room for me in it.

00:36:51.320 --> 00:36:56.719
And I know he'd never admit that, so...

00:36:56.719 --> 00:37:30.159
I just, um, break down the road.

00:37:30.159 --> 00:37:33.159
Besides, you know, why settle for hot, rich and famous

00:37:33.159 --> 00:37:56.670
when I can hang out with you?

00:37:56.670 --> 00:38:01.159
I guess you got Blondie's message, too.

00:38:01.159 --> 00:38:03.159
He spoke to Lois. I'm sorry about what happened.

00:38:03.159 --> 00:38:08.159
Maybe we should get used to the whole dual identity thing someday.

00:38:08.159 --> 00:38:10.159
Yeah, like when?

00:38:10.159 --> 00:38:13.159
When the Earth cracks open and time ticks backwards?

00:38:13.159 --> 00:38:17.650
I don't think so.

00:38:17.650 --> 00:38:19.650
Hey, thanks for coming.

00:38:19.650 --> 00:38:22.650
I guess I need to eat a little crow, huh?

00:38:22.650 --> 00:38:26.510
Is it too late to ask for an apology?

00:38:26.510 --> 00:38:28.510
Apology accepted.

00:38:28.510 --> 00:38:30.510
Assuming you stop moonlighting for legs.

00:38:30.510 --> 00:38:34.510
That won't be a problem. I've decided to hang out my fish nets.

00:38:34.510 --> 00:38:37.510
I think I was a little out of my league.

00:38:37.510 --> 00:38:38.510
I'll just stick to being the word of my legs.

00:38:38.510 --> 00:38:41.510
justice. At least I can't hurt anyone over the airways.

00:38:41.510 --> 00:38:43.510
Well, as long as they're not subsonic.

00:38:43.510 --> 00:38:47.510
Still, I gotta say, um, kind of seems like a waste.

00:38:47.510 --> 00:38:50.510
Besides, Oliver and his boys could always use a dead mother.

00:38:50.510 --> 00:38:52.510
It's true.

00:38:52.510 --> 00:38:54.510
I'm not really much of a team player.

00:38:54.510 --> 00:38:57.510
Really? That's perfect. You're gonna fit right in.

00:38:57.510 --> 00:39:03.409
What about you?

00:39:03.409 --> 00:39:07.409
I'd say ricocheting bullets off your back earns you the secret handshake.

00:39:07.409 --> 00:39:09.409
Maybe someday.

00:39:09.409 --> 00:39:11.409
Come on.

00:39:11.409 --> 00:39:12.409
Let's go.

00:39:12.409 --> 00:39:13.409
people I want you to meet.

00:39:13.409 --> 00:39:20.519
Is there no one ever told you you have lousy taste in women?

00:39:20.519 --> 00:39:21.519
Yeah.

00:39:21.519 --> 00:39:49.010
Hi.

00:39:49.010 --> 00:39:54.619
I talked to Chloe.

00:39:54.619 --> 00:40:09.920
I thought I should go stay with her for a few days.

00:40:09.920 --> 00:40:10.920
I stole a Lamborghini.

00:40:10.920 --> 00:40:19.909
I broke into a bank of ATM machines and I stole all the money.

00:40:19.909 --> 00:40:22.909
I ripped off more vault doors than I could count in a lifetime.

00:40:22.909 --> 00:40:26.909
Lana, I'm anything but perfect.

00:40:26.909 --> 00:40:35.679
And I know that it's hard to live with me, especially when not everyone can handle the double-sided life I live.

00:40:35.679 --> 00:40:40.329
I live.

00:40:40.329 --> 00:40:43.329
Clark, I've been a two-headed hydroly myself.

00:40:43.329 --> 00:40:51.489
It's funny, you can have all the right motives and still do all the wrong things.

00:40:51.489 --> 00:40:54.489
I just wish I knew how we ended up here.

00:40:54.489 --> 00:41:03.840
For what it's worth, I am still committed to us.

00:41:03.840 --> 00:41:08.489
You don't think I am.

00:41:08.489 --> 00:41:14.489
Clark, I think that you doubt whether I'm the one you're really going to end up with.

00:41:14.489 --> 00:41:22.539
I can't tell you the future, Lana.

00:41:22.539 --> 00:41:32.400
Honestly, I don't know what's going to happen to us, but I promise I'm going to do everything I can.

00:41:32.400 --> 00:41:35.400
I'm going to do everything I can to make sure that we can trust each other again.

00:41:35.400 --> 00:41:45.389
Just to be over.

